\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{The determinant action of a fixed connection}
\date{2026-11-01}

\p{Use a [connection background](fdip-006D) with its fixed invariant
fiber metric and mass #{m>0}. Let #{\mathbb K=\mathbb R} with an
orthogonal representation, or #{\mathbb K=\mathbb C} with a unitary
representation. The matter space is #{\mathcal H=F^V}, and
#{N=\dim_{\mathbb K}\mathcal H} includes the fiber dimension.
Write #{d\operatorname{vol}} for the induced real volume on this
space, of real dimension #{N} or #{2N}, respectively. Set
##{\begin{array}{c|cc}
\mathbb K&\kappa&d\nu\\\hline
\mathbb R&1/2&(2\pi)^{-N/2}d\operatorname{vol}\\
\mathbb C&1&\pi^{-N}d\operatorname{vol}
\end{array}}
and define the matter partition function and determinant action by
##{\begin{aligned}
Z_{\mathrm{mat}}(U)
 &=\int_{\mathcal H}e^{-\kappa\langle\phi,Q_U\phi\rangle}\,d\nu(\phi),\\
W(U)&=-\log Z_{\mathrm{mat}}(U).
\end{aligned}}
The connection is fixed in this integral; only #{\phi} is integrated.}

\p{Orthogonal or unitary diagonalization reduces the integral to
positive eigenvalues #{\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_N}. Each real
coordinate contributes #{\lambda_j^{-1/2}} by the
[real Gaussian integral](fdip-002T); each complex coordinate contributes
#{\lambda_j^{-1}} by the [complex integral](fdip-006I). Therefore
##{Z_{\mathrm{mat}}(U)=(\det_{\mathbb K}Q_U)^{-\kappa},\qquad
 W(U)=\kappa\log\det_{\mathbb K}Q_U.}
The determinant is positive even in the complex case, since #{Q_U}
is positive Hermitian. These reference measures make
#{Z_{\mathrm{mat}}=1} when #{Q_U=I}. The normalized matter law has
density #{Z_{\mathrm{mat}}(U)^{-1}e^{-\kappa\langle\phi,Q_U\phi\rangle}
with respect to #{\nu}, and covariance #{Q_U^{-1}} over the chosen
field. In the complex convention this means
#{\mathbb E[\phi\phi^*]=Q_U^{-1}}.}

\p{A gauge transformation acts unitarily on #{\mathcal H}, and
[gauge covariance](fdip-006E) gives
#{Q_{U^g}=T_gQ_UT_g^{-1}}. Thus #{W(U^g)=W(U)}. Unitary coordinate
changes also preserve the declared real volume. The metric, mass,
weights and graph remain supplied data; this determinant does not
choose them or yet define a probability law on connections.}
